# Accepted-risk register
# ----------------------
# Rules:
#   - Every entry MUST have: CVE ID, exp:YYYY-MM-DD, reason, approved-by, ticket
#   - After the expiry date Trivy reports the CVE again and the gate fails again.
#   - An empty file means no accepted risks. That is the correct default state.
#   - Never use this file to silence an entire severity class. One CVE, one line.
#
# Format:
#   CVE-XXXX-XXXXX exp:YYYY-MM-DD
#   # reason: <why it is not fixed right now>
#   # approved-by: <name and role>  ticket: <ticket ID>
#
# Example (do not uncomment unless you mean it):
#   # CVE-2024-99999 exp:2025-06-01
#   # reason: upstream fix not released; mitigated by network policy
#   # approved-by: M. Armah (lab owner)  ticket: LAB-001
